00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
some of the best environments that have  ever existed in the destiny world  appeared in the dreadnought the massive  warship dungeon and personal hellscape  of oryx the taken king exploring the  dreadnought was the peak of the original  destiny as it was both a horrifying  place to find yourself trapped in and a  delightfully dense landscape full of  mysteries to uncover in the upcoming  destiny 2 expansion the witch queen  players are again delving into the  throne world of a deadly hive god with  savithun's throne world developer bungie  looks to be pushing even harder on  creating a twisted locale filled with  frightening threats and deadly secrets  we recently got a chance to see about an  hour of the witch queen in action during  a hands off preview in which bungie took  us through the new destination  demonstrated some elements about the  expansion story campaign and showed how  things such as weapon crafting will work  like most destiny 2 destinations  savithun's throne world consists of  locations you'll run through as part of  the story campaign as well as public  areas you can explore at your leisure  the place looks to be comparable in size  to the dreaming city or the dreadnought  it'll consist of three public areas  linked together each with larger  structures you can enter and depths to  explore the screenshots and videos of  the throne world that bungie has already  shown off consist of hive structures and  dungeons swampy areas and a cleaner  white city-like landscape destiny 2  creative director joe blackburn said  during the presentation that the throne  world is a reflection of sabathun's mind  and thus these locations manifest  elements of her personality the desolate  swamps and dark halls of hive dungeons  represents sabathun's past her years as  a hive god and the species dedication to  death and conquest those things are  being supplanted by her more recent  desire for the light which is  represented by the city and its  cathedral from what we saw that seems  like it'll make different areas of the  throne world feel very distinct from one  another and may even represent different  objectives as you explore in the city  area you'll find the lucent brood  sabithun's light infused hive enemies  these have different characteristics  than the usual hive enemies even if  they're not the light-bearing hive  guardians we've been seeing in the  marketing for instance break the shield  of a lucent hive enemy and rather than  it exploding that shield will transform  into a moth made of light and quickly  try to find another enemy to cling to  and power up before you can shoot it  down if you venture too close the moth  will instead attack you flying toward  you to explode like a bomb meanwhile the  swampier parts of the throne world are  populated by enemies that might have  been left behind by sabathun's adoption  of the light the darker portions of the  throne world contain enemies like the  scorn those who served sabathune before  but who aren't as convinced about her  change in ideology it all suggests a  throne world that might be at war with  itself reflecting internal struggles  with sabathune that lines up with the  lore we've seen in the last year which  has shown sabathune struggling with  conflicting feelings bungie also showed  off a new mechanic that drives your  explorations of the throne world called  deep sight it allows guardians to see  things that are hidden in the throne  world whenever they interact with  specific nodes in the preview we saw  deep sight reveal platforms and pathways  since a big theme of the witch queen is  doing psychic detective work as bungie  has described it the deep sight mechanic  might be about more than just revealing  invisible platforms back in september  blackburn and justin truman destiny 2's  general manager described the witch  queen as containing the definitive  destiny 2 campaign and we got a sense of  what that means in action during the  preview as in past expansions starting  up the witch queen will throw you into a  story campaign that consists of multiple  quests each unlocking as you complete  the last these quests are going to see  major changes from past expansions  however blackburn wouldn't put much of  an exact length on the campaign in terms  of hours although he called this the  meatiest campaign in a long time in  destiny 2 and said it would clock in as  longer than that of beyond light the  additional length comes from bungie's  efforts to make the story missions  bigger and more involved than in the  past in fact story missions are  borrowing more from end game content  like raids and dungeons they'll  challenge you more and dish out more  rewards than past story missions have so  while they'll be longer it sounds like  they'll be worth replaying the added  rewards come in two flavors first story  missions consist of the usual run from  point a to point b structure we've seen  in the past at intervals though you'll  run into what bungie calls major  encounters these are moments like a boss  fight in a dungeon or a raid and you'll  know you're in for a challenge when you  see them the arena you'll be fighting in  will be obvious you'll be able to drop a  rally banner at the beginning of it to  refill your ammo and ability energy and  you'll get a chest for completing them  blackburn said story missions tend to  have two or three major encounters  although that count isn't uniform across  all of them so you'll be earning lots of  gear as you fight through the story the  second means for getting rewards is to  play the campaign on the new legendary  difficulty which will be about as tough  as legendary dungeons and raids and will  dish out more and better rewards bungie  said it believes destiny 2 veterans will  be able to solo the legendary version of  the story at the witch queen's launch  although it will be difficult the good  news is that the campaign features  selectable missions so you can switch  between difficulties as necessary with  the challenge scaling automatically with  the size of your fire team in fact you  will want to complete the campaign on  legendary eventually bungie said doing  so will earn you some additional rewards  although the developer didn't say what  they'll be  the witch queen isn't the only story  that'll be unfolding in destiny 2 at  launch as it has in the recent past  bungie is also launching the first  content season of 2022 alongside the  expansion which we now know is called  the season of the risen it dovetails  with the story of savithun's throne  world the lucid brood have appeared hive  guardians are on the loose and the solar  system at large is responding to this  new threat in fact the first person to  come to the vanguard's aid when these  new hive appear is keital the cabal  empress back in the season of the chosen  the vanguard and the cabal came to an  uneasy truce it looks like that  diplomacy has paid off although we have  no idea what the details of the story of  the season of the risen will be we do  know that you'll be getting some cabal  themed gear however the preview showed  off a couple of the new cabal guns for  the season and it appears that the  exotic weapon grand overture is also a  cabal weapon mimicking the missile  barrage of the cabal colossus enemy the  addition of origin traits the new perk  unique to specific sets of guns based on  where they come from means that the  cabal themed guns in the season of the  risen will have a new perk called land  tank that should be pretty useful to  players taking on tough content during  the early portion of the witch queen as  the trait will give you higher  resilience and damage resistance as you  rack up final blows with that gun we  don't know much else about the season of  the risen but it does suggest that like  the time loop in the dreaming city we'll  be dealing with what's going on in  sabathan's throne world for quite a  while among the other major additions to  destiny 2 with the witch queen is the  enclave where players will engage in the  new weapon crafting system the enclave  is a new physical location on mars which  somehow returns after somehow vanishing  at the end of season of the lost mars  won't be a large playable area but will  instead be similar to what phobos was  during the taken king expansion of  destiny 1. it looks to function a bit  like your base of operations for the  expansion and also houses a darkness  artifact called the relic which is where  weapon crafting takes place bungie  showed us a bit more about how weapon  crafting will work expanding on the  recent this week at bungie blog post  that ran the system down in order to get  guns you can craft you'll need to unlock  patterns to get those you'll hunt for  random drop versions of the guns you  want ones that have a red border on  their icon  this means the weapon comes with deep  sight resonance which is the key  requirement to crafting the deepsite  resonance guns come with objectives to  complete by using them which will have  you taking on activities and racking up  kills completing those objectives will  either earn you a pattern for the gun or  currency that you'll use for crafting  once you have a pattern you can craft  your own version of the gun and then add  the perks you want to it although not  every gun can carry every perk much like  the random rules you get on weapons  right now you'll also need to use the  crafted gun in order to level it up and  as you do more perks will become  available to it it seems like there will  be a lot of currencies involved with the  crafting system we counted at least four  during the presentation although it's  not clear what they all do or how tough  to acquire they'll be destiny has  definitely had issues with including  tons of confusing super specific  currencies in the past so that's a  potential drawback with the crafting  system we'll have to see how it actually  feels and functions by playing it and  like everything in destiny 2 it's  entirely possible bungie will adjust it  once players have had it in their hands  for a bit if the currencies get unwieldy  you should also know that not every  weapon will be craftable at the launch  of witch queen but there are no time  gates or upper limits on how many  weapons you can craft at the relic the  only limiting factor is how many  materials you have blackburn said bungie  isn't looking to make weapon crafting a  situation that's about making 10 000  daggers just to get one good one instead  you're going to be making very  deliberate choices about the weapons you  make and bungie wants you to develop a  relationship with that weapon the  crafting system will even track the date  you shaped your gun and will note its  level as you use it what's more the  relic allows you to craft guns to shape  them and then to recraft or reshape them  in essence you won't have to keep three  or four copies of the same gun with  different perks in your vault just in  case one roll ends up becoming meta when  bungie makes changes to the destiny 2  sandbox instead you can take the one gun  you made that you like return to the  relic and change its perks around with  the reshape option it's still the same  gun you've come to love but crafting  will allow it to be adaptable to changes  in the game finally we got a very quick  taste of bungie's coming adjustments to  the void subclasses the first set of  changes that are coming to the light  classes that have been part of destiny 2  since its release when bungie released  stasis with beyond light it also  introduced a new more involved user  interface for the subclass that allowed  for greater customization with elements  called fragments and aspects that system  is coming to the other subclasses  although one at a time and the first up  is void the new void interface looks  almost exactly like the stasis one and  it sounds like it'll function in the  same way with players earning aspects  and fragments to further customize their  subclasses to their playstyles in its  witch queen vidoc bungie devs joked that  all players will now be able to use  suppression grenades and to some degree  elements that used to be reserved to a  certain class are being democratized to  all through the use of aspects and  fragments we don't have too many other  details on the void 3.0 system but  bungie noted that players who've been in  the game for a while will have instant  access to everything they currently use  to make up their void subclasses in  other words you won't need to re-unlock  your standard void grenades or melee  attacks you'll have them as soon as you  log into the game as for the newer  editions bungie isn't going to gate them  too hard for players who've been in the  game for a while there will be a place  in the tower you can visit to upgrade  your void subclass for currency so you  won't have to go on lengthy quests to  earn the new elements coming to the  system you'll be able to enjoy it  quickly but we're not yet sure who  you'll have to visit or what you'll need  to spend to get these new void elements  there's a whole lot about the witch  queen we don't yet know but bungie's  preview event at least gave a sense of  what the new expansion will be like the  additions to weapons and classes look  like significant improvements and there  will be plenty to uncover in savithun's  throne world guardians will have to  uncover anything more than that by  themselves when the witch queen launches  on february 22nd  you

